194139535298 true] [17592186342459 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535298 true] [17592186342459 1111 #uuid "acc9b635-0429-5911-b2d2-6c43fcdb8972" 13194139535298 true] [17592186342460 1017 #edb/ref 17592186342461 13194139535298 true] [17592186342460 1089 "q-126710" 13194139535298 true] [17592186342460 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535298 true] [17592186342460 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061894/assets/831b2131cf134ec21def0014a3121429ded4cd3afd98dfd1660b1e78c1a9ba93.png)\n\nConsider the path $C$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y)=⟨y(x+1),\\,x(y+1)⟩,$ which of the following is equivalent to ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot dr\\,?$" 13194139535298 true] [17592186342460 1113 #uuid "bb455109-e1d6-5470-bd07-6efd0cad0f45" 13194139535298 true] [17592186342460 1145 "First, notice that we can rewrite our integral as \n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot dr={∮}_{C}y(x+1)\\,dx+x(y+1)\\,dy.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the region $D$ and its boundary $C$ satisfy the conditions of Green's theorem:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061894/assets/d8cd55f88d614bdb49aee6eaa0ff9d1d56f6f597cd892ee199a0130b53954b5b.png)\n\nSince $P(x,y)=y(x+1)$ and $Q(x,y)=x(y+1),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=x+1,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=y+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}y(x+1)\\,dx+x(y+1)\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(y+1-(x+1))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(y-x)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the region $D$ can be represented in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 3,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{3\\pi }{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe change of variables formula for plane polar coordinates states that  \n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our double integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}(y-x)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{3}{r}^{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\,dr\\,d\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535298 true] [17592186342461 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342462 13194139535298 true] [17592186342461 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342463 13194139535298 true] [17592186342461 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342464 13194139535298 true] [17592186342461 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342465 13194139535298 true] [17592186342461 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342466 13194139535298 true] [17592186342461 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535298 true] [17592186342461 1041 "selection" 13194139535298 true] [17592186342461 1104 #edb/ref 17592186342464 13194139535298 true] [17592186342461 1110 #uuid "6c1c714e-755b-5c86-9d96-ac4f040ad314" 13194139535298 true] [17592186342462 1034 "{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{3}r(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,dr\\,d\\theta " 13194139535298 true] [17592186342462 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535298 true] [17592186342462 1111 #uuid "c56c7af3-f761-50a1-95ea-382c8e1b41be" 13194139535298 true] [17592186342463 1034 "{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{3}{r}^{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,dr\\,d\\theta " 13194139535298 true] [17592186342463 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535298 true] [17592186342463 1111 #uuid "f22e6a42-5a4e-5ae8-aca2-662068740153" 13194139535298 true] [17592186342464 1034 "{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{3}{r}^{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\,dr\\,d\\theta " 13194139535298 true] [17592186342464 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 131941395