)=xy+y{e}^{y},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=2y,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}({y}^{2}+{x}^{2})\\,dx+(xy+y{e}^{y})\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(y-2y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}-y\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the region $D$ can be represented in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 1,\\,-\\pi \\le \\theta \\le 0}.\n$$\n\nThe change of variables formula for plane polar coordinates states that \n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our double integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}-y\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}-r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{0}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{1}-{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,dr\\,d\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535298 true] [17592186342468 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342469 13194139535298 true] [17592186342468 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342470 13194139535298 true] [17592186342468 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342471 13194139535298 true] [17592186342468 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342472 13194139535298 true] [17592186342468 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342473 13194139535298 true] [17592186342468 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535298 true] [17592186342468 1041 "selection" 13194139535298 true] [17592186342468 1104 #edb/ref 17592186342469 13194139535298 true] [17592186342468 1110 #uuid "be037c5f-38be-5ef0-9f94-f862bace0450" 13194139535298 true] [17592186342469 1034 "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{0}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{1}-{r}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,dr\\,d\\theta " 13194139535298 true] [17592186342469 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535298 true] [17592186342469 1111 #uuid "3cc1e2ef-b956-5042-b916-958ba311dacb" 13194139535298 true] [17592186342470 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{1}-r