presented in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 2,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nThe change of variables formula for plane polar coordinates states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nFinally, we can calculate our double integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}({r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{3}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }[\\frac{{r}^{4}}{4}]_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }4\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =4[\\theta ]_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =4(2\\pi -0) \\\\  & =8\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535298 true] [17592186342503 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342504 13194139535298 true] [17592186342503 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342505 13194139535298 true] [17592186342503 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342506 13194139535298 true] [17592186342503 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342507 13194139535298 true] [17592186342503 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342508 13194139535298 true] [17592186342503 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535298 true] [17592186342503 1041 "selection" 13194139535298 true] [17592186342503 1104 #edb/ref 17592186342505 13194139535298 true] [17592186342503 1110 #uuid "8f842549-db89-54f2-80f9-144a874f42e4" 13194139535298 true] [17592186342504 1034 "4\\pi " 13194139535298 true] [17592186342504 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535298 true] [17592186342504 1111 #uuid "b4f08eaf-8bbd-53a8-bb20-1b26665df76a" 13194139535298 true] [17592186342505 1034 "8\\pi " 13194139535298 true] [17592186342505 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535298 true] [17592186342505 1111 #uuid "732018aa-6936-534d-ab88-b0d77ca1dfd2" 131941